From 41c5fb5a72abb13468c36c547acd78384ad61432 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:10:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(sim,motion,app): judge turning, rotary and 5-axis
 ball kinds on a reduced-fidelity model; the collision laws read its excess

#864 tightened the upright mill kinds' gouge laws by a coarse model's
excess (its chord error past the importer's promise) and refused every
other kind outright. The rule is unchanged - a tolerance gives the excess
back while a positive tolerance is left, the gate refuses by name past
that - and now reaches:

- Turning, band kinds: the meridian scan's gouge clause
  (turning::gouge_tol_on; blade/thread/form `_warnings_excess`), and the
  composed blade scan that judges a Part's inspection ask at the post.
- Every turning kind: the meridian rapid, bar-feed and holder margin.
- Rotary kinds: the radial field law's band and rapid allowances.
- Turning nose kinds and the multi-axis ball kinds were already judged
  by the envelope law (f), which #864 tightened; they are taken off the
  refused list.
- Collision laws in verify: shank/holder reach (c) and its mid-turn
  sweep (c3) grow their bands by the excess and shrink the kerf; rapids
  in stock (d) and its posed reading give the excess back.

The gate's floor is per kind (the smallest tolerance any of its laws
holds, a Part's inspection ask included), and an operation is judged
with the worse of its source's and its setup stock's excess.

Still refused, for a stated reason: swarf (the flank is proved only in
the generator), the cone and engrave rides, probe, the cross drill and
plasma.

Structure only, for the 400-line law: turning/blade_law.rs and
turning/thread_law.rs split from revolve.rs and thread.rs,
verify/excess.rs from verify/types.rs.

Refs #904

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
